# knowledge-management-model

The knowledge management system organizes domain expertise across three key hierarchies:

## Practice Categories & Mappings (Importance: 85/100)
- Treatment protocols mapped to specific intervention categories
- Evidence-based practice classifications 
- Regional prioritization and local partnership categorization
- Service capability tagging system

## Best Practices Integration (Importance: 90/100)
File: components/knowledge/BestPracticesManager.tsx
- Clinical guidelines organized by treatment domain
- Trauma-informed care principles mapping
- Context-aware formatting for AI prompt integration
- Multi-faceted search across organizational protocols

## Local Resource Classification (Importance: 80/100)
File: components/knowledge/LocalPartnershipsManager.tsx
- Treatment provider categorization by service type:
  - Detox centers
  - Halfway houses
  - Outpatient facilities
  - Residential treatment
  - Community resources
- ZIP code-based regional organization
- Service flag mapping system
- Referral pathway tracking

Core Domain Organization:
1. Treatment Protocols
2. Clinical Guidelines
3. Evidence-Based Practices
4. Local Partnerships
5. Regional Resources
6. Service Capabilities

The system maintains relationships between knowledge domains while supporting:
- Context-aware knowledge retrieval
- Domain-specific categorization
- Treatment-to-provider mapping
- Regional resource organization
- Best practice integration

